cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research software, please cite it as the OwlPath Project Team.
  The project founder and clinical lead is the founder of DR.ECC; their verified
  identity has been disclosed to the competition organizers and is intentionally
  not displayed in this public repository.
title: "OwlPath: a development-first multi-specialty agent system for pathogen hypothesis generation"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - name: "OwlPath Project Team"
repository-code: "https://github.com/188097259-web/OwlPath"
url: "https://github.com/188097259-web/OwlPath"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  OwlPath is a local web research prototype that coordinates specialty agents,
  evidence retrieval, pathogen hypothesis synthesis, deterministic output
  validation, and independent review. It is intended for software development,
  competition demonstration, and methods research only. It is not a medical
  device and has not completed clinical validation.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - clinical research software
  - infectious diseases
  - pathogen hypothesis generation
  - multi-agent systems
